    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `contactPreference` rule: **`EMAIL`** when an email address is present, otherwise **`PHONE`**.\n\nI followed the codebase's existing pattern for derived, read-only owner response fields (like `locality`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`), which are computed by getters on the `Owner` model and auto-mapped into the response DTO by MapStruct:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (this generates the corresponding field on `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getContactPreference()` getter returning `\"EMAIL\"` when a non-blank email is present, else `\"PHONE\"`. MapStruct picks it up automatically (no mapper change needed).\n\nResults:\n- `Cp27Tests` (both the no-email \u2192 `PHONE` and email-present \u2192 `EMAIL` cases) passes.\n- Full suite: **38 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.",
